{
 "id": "2024-jin-scenic",
 "name": "Scenic Beauty of Waterfront Planting",
 "description": "Scenic Beauty Estimation (SBE) of a historic Chinese garden: participants see 32 waterfront plant landscape units in Xingqing Palace Park, Xi'an, each shown as two photos, and rate each from 1 to 5 (poor landscape effect, average, fairly good, good, high scenic beauty). The paper's raw ratings from 100 respondents (landscape/aesthetics teachers and students plus on-site visitors) are open in its S3 File, so a new sample can be compared unit by unit, and SBE scores (S = 5 × Σ j·n_j/N) can be computed in the same way. Rebuilt from Jin & Miao (2024), PLOS ONE 19(5): e0302855, using the authors' CC BY photos (S1 Fig). Differences from the original study: (1) English wording; the five anchors are translated from the original questionnaire (the paper's English text describes level 3 differently); (2) unit order is randomised per participant (the paper does not report its order); (3) the 'which describes you best' and gender questions are added to mirror the reported sample (students/teachers vs visitors, 50% female); the original questionnaire's other background items are not published; (4) the Delphi/AHP expert stage of the paper is not part of this template.",
